\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Still, still with Thee, when
\par purple morning breaketh,
\par When the bird waketh, and the
\par shadows flee;
\par Fairer than morning, lovelier
\par than daylight,
\par Dawns the sweet consciousness,
\par I am with Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Alone with Thee, amid the mystic 
\par shadows,
\par The solemn hush of nature
\par newly born;
\par Alone with Thee in breathless
\par adoration,
\par In the calm dew and freshness
\par of the morn.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. As in the dawning, o'er the waveless
\par ocean,
\par The image of the morning star
\par doth rest;
\par So in this stillness, Thou beholdest
\par only
\par Thine image in the waters of my 
\par breast.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Still, still with Thee! As to each
\par newborn morning
\par A fresh and solemn splendour still
\par is given;
\par So does this blessed consciousness, 
\par awaking,
\par Breathe each day nearness unto
\par Thee and heaven.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. When sinks the soul, subdued by
\par toil to slumber,
\par Its closing eye looks up to Thee
\par in prayer;
\par Sweet the repose beneath Thy
\par wings o'ershading,
\par But sweeter still, to wake and 
\par find Thee there.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. So shall it be at last, in that
\par bright morning,
\par When the soul waketh, and life's
\par shadow flee;
\par O in that hour, fairer than 
\par daylight dawning,
\par Shall rise the glorious thought
\par - I am with Thee! \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

